# Build context exclusions for `docker build`.
#
# The image is built FROM SOURCE in the build stage (tsc), so nothing generated or vendored in a
# checkout needs to reach the daemon. A smaller context is also a smaller chance of shipping a
# secret or a stale artifact into a layer.

# Dependencies: reinstalled inside the build stage from package-lock.json.
**/node_modules

# Build output: the build stage produces its own; a stale local dist/ must never be what ships.
**/dist

# VCS metadata and history.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Audit bundles: generated evidence with per-run timestamps, never part of an image.
.sdd/audit
**/.sdd/audit

# Bench output (the harness writes into a temp dir; these cover anything dumped next to it).
bench/out
bench/results
bench/*.json
bench/**/*.json

# Local, machine-specific and editor state.
.sdd/settings/security-allowlist.local.json
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.log

# Docs and other non-build inputs: kept out of the context on purpose. Uncomment `docs` if you
# want to COPY documentation into the image.
docs
README.md
README-OPENSDD.md
CHANGELOG.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
assets
